  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 209 AM CDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nEarlier in the night, there was some considerable flash flooding \nthat occurred north of I-72. Some showers and thunderstorms are \nstill moving across central and southeastern IL this morning but the \nflash flooding threat appears to have ended. Heavy rain is still \npossible in the stronger showers as this cold front exits off to the \nsouth this morning. \n\nBehind the cold front, a weak high pressure center will build over \nthe Midwest later today into tomorrow. Today is looking to be quite \npleasant. There could be some sprinkles/light rain in south central \nIL this afternoon, but rainfall amounts should be minimal. Friday \nthere is a 20-40% chance of additional showers, perhaps some thunder \ntoo, area wide as a weak upper disturbance passes overhead. \n\nAfter Friday, a primarily dry forecast is on deck through early next \nweek, with temperatures in the upper 70s to 80s for highs and \nupper 50s to 60s for lows.",
